# Shared agent taskboard (mandatory)

Follow protocol in [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). Your agent name here: **`cursor`**. Event brief: [`HACKATHON.md`](../../HACKATHON.md).

Before inspecting or modifying files for a request:

1. Run `./scripts/agent-taskboard.sh context --agent cursor` and read [`agent-coordination/taskboard.md`](../../agent-coordination/taskboard.md).
2. Unfinished task covers request: continue that same task, even if Claude Code or Codex created it:
   `./scripts/agent-taskboard.sh take-over --agent cursor --task "<task-id>"`
3. Otherwise register one:
   `./scripts/agent-taskboard.sh start --agent cursor --title "<title>" --scope "<paths>"`
   then fill its `plan.md` before editing.
4. Checkpoint at milestones (`checkpoint ... --summary ... --next ...`). `complete` only after validation.

`afterAgentResponse` hook records a checkpoint on your active task and commits the turn (pushed automatically). End every response with exactly one line:

```text
Taskboard checkpoint: <what changed, key result, or blocker> | Next: <single next action>
```

Never edit `taskboard.md` by hand or overwrite another task's plan.
